### Describe the bug

Hello,

as written in the title, I recently installed a freshly compiled update for lawnchair, and now the double tap to suspend in homescreen doens't work anymore through root. I have to enable the accessibility service, and suspending this way is slower and a little bit glitchy (screen turns on for a second after locking).

Thanks for your support

### Steps to reproduce

1. Enable "suspend" function in gestures
2. Double tap to suspend

### Expected behavior

I expect the screen to shut off instantly, as it was using root.

Now instead it required to enable accessibility service; then, after I double tap, the screen locks, turns on for a second, and turns off again.

